\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Under the converged recipe.}{11}{section*.28}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Paper task under the converged torus recipe (300 epochs, 5\% warmup + cosine, lr $10^{-3}$). Metric: accuracy of predicting the observation at revisited cells, on a map not seen in training; trained at $T=128$, evaluated at $T=128$, 512 and 1024 (eight times the training length). 6 arms $\times $ 8 seeds in one batch, pre-registered (\texttt  {PAPER2X2\_PREREG.md}). Arms cross two factors. \emph  {Enc.} (encoding): RoPE = rotation only; PoPE = PoPE's content-dependent magnitude with a rotation. \emph  {Position} (what sets the rotation angle): index = the token's index, as in a standard transformer; path-int.\ = MapFormer's running sum of learned per-token increments, through a bottleneck of rank $r$. \texttt  {Vanilla} = MapFormer-WM; \texttt  {RoPE} = MapFormer with index rotation. Top rows: accuracy mean $\pm $ sd; final training loss as mean (range over seeds). Bottom rows: main effects on accuracy at the stated rank, paired by seed, given as effect (\textsc  {mde}, seeds with a positive difference). \emph  {Position} = path-integrated minus index, averaged over the two encodings; \emph  {encoding} = PoPE minus RoPE, averaged over the two position sources; the two index arms serve both ranks. \textsc  {mde} = minimum detectable effect, $2.8\,\mathrm  {sd}/\sqrt  {n}$ on the paired differences; every main effect shown exceeds its \textsc  {mde} (detectable). Effects are on raw accuracy; no position effect at matched final training loss is reported, because index and path-integrated arms end training at non-overlapping losses (see text). Blank floor (always predicting blank) about 0.51 at $T=128$ (0.506 measured on a different evaluator's events). Reading: path integration is the larger factor at every length; the encoding is detectably negative at training length and adds a smaller, detectable amount beyond it.\relax }}{12}{table.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:paper2x2-converged}{{9}{12}{Paper task under the converged torus recipe (300 epochs, 5\% warmup + cosine, lr $10^{-3}$). Metric: accuracy of predicting the observation at revisited cells, on a map not seen in training; trained at $T=128$, evaluated at $T=128$, 512 and 1024 (eight times the training length). 6 arms $\times $ 8 seeds in one batch, pre-registered (\texttt {PAPER2X2\_PREREG.md}). Arms cross two factors. \emph {Enc.} (encoding): RoPE = rotation only; PoPE = PoPE's content-dependent magnitude with a rotation. \emph {Position} (what sets the rotation angle): index = the token's index, as in a standard transformer; path-int.\ = MapFormer's running sum of learned per-token increments, through a bottleneck of rank $r$. \texttt {Vanilla} = MapFormer-WM; \texttt {RoPE} = MapFormer with index rotation. Top rows: accuracy mean $\pm $ sd; final training loss as mean (range over seeds). Bottom rows: main effects on accuracy at the stated rank, paired by seed, given as effect (\textsc {mde}, seeds with a positive difference). \emph {Position} = path-integrated minus index, averaged over the two encodings; \emph {encoding} = PoPE minus RoPE, averaged over the two position sources; the two index arms serve both ranks. \textsc {mde} = minimum detectable effect, $2.8\,\mathrm {sd}/\sqrt {n}$ on the paired differences; every main effect shown exceeds its \textsc {mde} (detectable). Effects are on raw accuracy; no position effect at matched final training loss is reported, because index and path-integrated arms end training at non-overlapping losses (see text). Blank floor (always predicting blank) about 0.51 at $T=128$ (0.506 measured on a different evaluator's events). Reading: path integration is the larger factor at every length; the encoding is detectably negative at training length and adds a smaller, detectable amount beyond it.\relax }{table.caption.27}{}}
